;; holds a source-lava pool, the walkable rim one block above it. Rebuilt from the body's recorded chunks around
;; [112..131, -55..-51, 46..64] (plot = world x-108, y+54, z-42; the rim floor y -55 is the plot floor y -1).
;; The pocket [16 0 7] [15 0 8] [15 0 9] joins the cave only by corner slides whose open side is a hole onto the
;; lava ([16 0 8] and [15 0 10]); the planner made them as plain corner slides and the slide carried the body over
;; the lava 2 of 2 times. After the planner fix such a slide costs HAZARD-SLIDE-RISK (10 hp): a walk that has a way round
;; never takes it (no :hurt by lava); a walk out of or into the pocket still takes it (the only way) and arrives. The
;; walker hops those slides (executor :hop, card 74a8cee4), so even then the body takes no lava :hurt.
